WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.210
Choose the right format, get your phone ready, and protect privacy.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.720
This is the video for module one of Voice Notes, Photos and Videos for Expression.

3
00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:17.250
Your phone gives you four ways to send a message: typed text, a voice note, a photo and a video.

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:27.140
No format is best for everything. A woman who always types may send three long paragraphs about a leaking pipe, when one photo would do.

5
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:35.020
You do not need an expensive phone. You need to know where things are, and how much data each kind of media takes.

6
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.310
And before any recording skill come habits that protect you and the people you record.

7
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:52.350
Typed text carries exact details: numbers, names and times, easy to copy later. A photo shows what something looks like, but does not explain.

8
00:00:53.600 --> 00:01:03.350
A voice note carries tone and warmth, but numbers are hard to copy from it. A video shows movement, steps and a route, and it is the heaviest on data.

9
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:15.560
First: must the listener copy or keep an exact detail, like a number, an address or an amount? Then that detail goes in text, even if the rest is a voice note.

10
00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.460
Second: does the message depend on what something looks like? Then add a photo.

11
00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:29.260
Third: does it depend on movement, order or sound, like the route from the junction? Then a short video.

12
00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:38.470
Fourth: does it depend on feeling or tone, like thanks, an apology or a delicate request? Then a voice note, or a call.

13
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:49.150
There is a fifth option: do not record at all. A recording can be forwarded and taken out of context. For a quarrel or bad news, call or visit.

14
00:01:50.400 --> 00:02:00.890
For example, Halima in Kaduna has water dripping from her bathroom ceiling after rain. Her landlord is an elderly man who prefers calls and voice notes.

15
00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:07.110
She types the exact details: Flat 3B, leak started Tuesday 14th after the rain.

16
00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:17.510
She takes two photos: one wide shot of the whole ceiling, and one close-up of the drip. A video would add little, so she skips it to save data.

17
00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:28.960
He likes to be greeted properly, so she records a 25-second voice note. She sends it first, then the photos, then the typed line he can forward to the plumber.

18
00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:41.650
A one-minute voice note is usually well under 1 MB. A camera photo is often 2 to 6 MB. One minute of full HD video is often 50 MB or more.

19
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.070
In WhatsApp, open Settings, then Storage and data.

20
00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:55.580
Under Media auto-download, set mobile data to download nothing, or photos only. Videos will then wait until you tap them.

21
00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:05.640
Manage storage shows the chats using the most space, so you can delete big old files. But back up first, and never delete without looking.

22
00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:11.670
Keep a few gigabytes free before an important recording, such as a family event.

23
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:20.430
Consent means the person agrees freely, knowing where the recording will go. For children, ask the parent or guardian.

24
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:32.830
Then run six checks. Did they agree? Do they know where it goes? Background checked for house numbers or school badges? No cards or PINs? Location tag off? Fine if forwarded?

25
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:43.060
Some things must never be photographed or recorded: your ATM card number or the three digits on its back, and your BVN or NIN.

26
00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:51.120
Also PINs, one-time passwords, which we call OTPs, other passwords, and full bank statements.

27
00:03:52.370 --> 00:04:01.780
No genuine bank, network or government office will ask you to send these as a photo, voice note or video. If someone asks, treat it as a scam.

28
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:11.770
To remember. Text for exact details, photo for looks, video for steps, and a voice note for tone, with the key number typed underneath.

29
00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:19.850
Turn off video auto-download on mobile data. Ask before you record anyone, and check every background before you send.

30
00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:37.160
Now practise. Audit the format of your last ten messages. Do a phone readiness check and write down your file sizes and free storage. Turn off location tags and set your Status privacy. And run the six checks on three photos you shared.

31
00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.450
Continue with the lessons below.
